From: ginux-watch-agent <actions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 13:57:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(kernel-views): pin /etc/hostname read and ns/pid +
 ns/uts readlink targets

### What
Pins three IdentityFs arms: reading `/etc/hostname` returns the instance hostname with a trailing newline, and `readlink` on `ns/pid` / `ns/uts` renders `pid:[id]` / `uts:[id]` with the instance-owned namespace ids.

### Why it matters
Userspace reads hostname and namespace links to detect isolation. Deleting any of these match arms turns a valid path into NotFound, breaking hostname resolution and namespace introspection. The existing identity test pins machine-id, ns/mnt and ns/cgroup only, so all three deletions survive it.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| delete `/etc/hostname` read arm | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| delete `ns/pid` readlink arm | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| delete `ns/uts` readlink arm | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline (clean tree + new test): PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-kernel-views --lib identity_hostname_read_and_pid_uts`.

Spec-Ref: proc(5) namespace symlinks (ns/pid, ns/uts); hostname(7) via /etc/hostname

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/lib.rs | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/lib.rs
index 950b5a89..8c6c4106 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-kernel-views/src/lib.rs
@@ -600,6 +600,38 @@ mod tests {
         assert!(sysfs.read(b"/sys/class/net/net0/type", &mut output).is_ok());
     }
 
+    #[test]
+    fn identity_hostname_read_and_pid_uts_namespace_links_are_exact() {
+        let (tasks, count) = fixture();
+        let identity = IdentityView {
+            hostname: b"instance-a",
+            machine_id: b"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef",
+            boot_id: b"11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555",
+        };
+        let identities = IdentityFs::new(
+            &tasks[..count],
+            identity,
+            NamespaceView {
+                mount: 101,
+                pid: 102,
+                uts: 103,
+                cgroup: 104,
+            },
+        );
+        let mut output = [0u8; 128];
+        let len = identities.read(b"/etc/hostname", &mut output).unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(&output[..len], b"instance-a\n");
+        let len = identities.readlink(b"/proc/1/ns/pid", &mut output).unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(&output[..len], b"pid:[102]");
+        let len = identities.readlink(b"/proc/1/ns/uts", &mut output).unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(&output[..len], b"uts:[103]");
+        // unknown namespace leaf still NotFound
+        assert_eq!(
+            identities.readlink(b"/proc/1/ns/net", &mut output),
+            Err(ViewError::NotFound)
+        );
+    }
+
     #[test]
     fn sysfs_projects_only_assigned_virtual_devices() {
         let mut registry: DeviceRegistry<6, 2> = DeviceRegistry::new();
